From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:33:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: sunxi: mbus: add the A10/A20 mixer processor

The A20 mixer processor (2D engine) is an MBUS master. Like the display
engine, the video engine and the Mali GPU it sees DRAM at bus address 0
rather than at PHYS_OFFSET, so it needs the same DMA offset. The legacy
3.4 driver subtracted 0x40000000 from every address it programmed.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c
index 60b670585..eb374d47f 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@ static const char * const sunxi_mbus_devices[] = {
 	"allwinner,sun4i-a10-display-backend",
 	"allwinner,sun4i-a10-display-frontend",
 	"allwinner,sun4i-a10-mali",
+	"allwinner,sun4i-a10-mixer-processor",
 	"allwinner,sun4i-a10-video-engine",
 	"allwinner,sun5i-a13-display-backend",
 	"allwinner,sun5i-a13-video-engine",
-- 
